const nums = ['1', '2', '3'];
console.log(nums == 1);
console.log(nums[0] == 1);

output:
**Issue:** Loose equality (==) triggers type coercion.
**Why:** The string array coerces to '123', which is not 1, while nums[0] == 1 is true only because of coercion; the mixed results hide real type errors.
**Fix:**
const nums = ['1', '2', '3'];
console.log(nums === '1,2,3');
console.log(Number(nums[0]) === 1);

